    q: "Which is better, battery or plug-in?",
    a: "Neither wins outright, and the answer is that backup is what actually matters. A plug-in unit never dies because someone pulled the battery for a TV remote, but it stops in an outage. A battery unit survives the outage but depends on someone remembering it exists. What you want is either type with a backup power source, because the window when carbon monoxide risk peaks — a generator running, an outage, a storm, everyone indoors — is exactly the window when mains power is least reliable.",
